    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Behind the technical name Isomap, what intuitive problem were researchers confronting?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Joshua Tenenbaum, Vin de Silva, and John Langford introduced Isomap for nonlinear dimensionality reduction. It builds a neighborhood graph, estimates geodesic distances along that graph, and embeds the data to preserve global manifold geometry.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-global-geometric-framework-for-nonlinear-dimensionality-reduction"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Local neighbor edges approximate geodesic distances, then a global embedding unfolds the manifold.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-global-geometric-framework-for-nonlinear-dimensionality-reduction"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat Isomap as a landmark manifold-learning method because it made global nonlinear geometry operational. Its long-term legacy is the graph-distance view of representation learning, later echoed in visualization and graph-based learning methods.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-a-global-geometric-framework-for-nonlinear-dimensionality-reduction"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "SUMMARY",
            "text": "Isomap mattered not only as a result, but as a method that later researchers could test, adapt, and extend.",
